  "body": "Logotype (the maintainer's artwork, used as given) as the app window icon, in the README and as the site favicon.\n\nWhat changed\n- `assets/logo/camcraft-logo.png` is the source. `cargo xtask logo [--check]` (new, `xtask/src/logo.rs`) pads it to a square and writes 16-512 px PNGs and `camcraft.ico` to `assets/logo/icons/`. No new dependency: tiny-skia via the resvg xtask already has; `docs/decisions/1459-logotype.md` records it.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/app_icon.rs`: the 128 px icon is decoded and set on the native window (`with_window_icon`).\n- README shows the logotype at the top; `assets/ui/LICENSES.md` says it is the maintainer's own artwork; `site/static/favicon.png` plus one link in `site/templates/base.html`.\n- `PROCESS_VERSION` 60 -> 61 (xtask changed).\n\nPinned by: `the_logotype_icon_decodes_square_and_opaque` (camcraft-ui lib), `committed_logo_sizes_match_the_source`, `ico_header_and_offsets_are_consistent`, `a_wide_source_is_padded_to_a_square` (xtask). Gate: those, whole xtask suite (115 pass), clippy on xtask and camcraft-ui clean.\n\nNot done here (scripts/, build.rs, .github): Windows exe/installer icon, macOS .icns, Linux desktop icons; follow-up filed (see the issue). Needs a build dependency or script edits, so the maintainer's yes.\n\nNot exercised: the icon was not looked at in the running app, and the site was not built with zola; a screenshot of the taskbar/title bar is owed by the maintainer. No snapshot PNG touched.\n\nChangelog: The CamCraft logotype is the window icon, the README header and the site favicon (#1459, PR #M)\nEffort: medium\n\nRefs #1459\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
